refore it's  better to be in the office but as long  as the person has a room where they can  isolate themselves they can have the  zoom calls or  productive they can work from anywhere  they want and so the idea is to have  this nice combination of  limited time but we're all together  and time where we can work from home and  we can be at our own pace  yeah that's great  um  okay so i'm looking at the clock what i  think we will do is i'll share i wanted  to share a little bit about the program  that brought all of us uh here together  uh so i'll take a couple of minutes to  do that and then i hope we'll have time  for uh one or two more questions so um  the the program that is really  sponsoring this uh panel conversation  today is a program we call leading from  home  managing remote teams and hybrid uh  teams and uh  uh all of the our our uh panelists here  on the webinar today have participated  in that program  and the the program it's been very  interesting we we launched it our center  launched it right uh very closely after  the pandemic started and as we've  delivered multiple cohorts of that  program we've been uh evolving both in  terms of the research that we're  presenting and the things that are being  discovered about remote and hybrid work  as well as the types of challenges that  we see managers and leaders that join  the program are facing  and so here is a brief snapshot of what  the  program covers so this is a live virtual  program it's fully live  in the program we have faculty that are  presenting but just as important i think  we have many opportunities for the  participants and learners  to have a dialogue amongst themselves we  have many breakout rooms and and q a and  conversations and you're seeing a little  bit of that in the session today where a  lot of the knowledge and learning can  happen just by engaging with kind of  motivated and curious and and passionate  peers that are really trying to perfect  their their personal managemen